00:15:52,560 --> 00:15:53,640
Typical old man

253
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:57,137
He's squeezing a cotton ball between
his finger and the coin to leak

254
00:15:57,220 --> 00:16:01,338
liquid into the glass So that's how
he's gonna make the glass overflow

255
00:16:01,800 --> 00:16:03,940
And he told me to watch for cheating

256
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:05,800
clever bastard

257
00:16:06,420 --> 00:16:07,250
Not bad.

258
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:19,160
The glass has reached its limit!

259
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:21,657
One more coin and the booze will spill!

260
00:16:21,740 --> 00:16:22,800
Victory is mine!

261
00:16:23,340 --> 00:16:27,620
It's like he said, we'll see
which dance partner cries first.

262
00:16:28,540 --> 00:16:30,480
Ooh, man, that was a close one.

263
00:16:30,660 --> 00:16:32,457
I thought it was gonna spill for sure.

264
00:16:32,540 --> 00:16:35,000
Well, it's your turn. Good luck, Obi.

265
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:38,360
It's Darby!

266
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:40,088
Don't make me say it again!

267
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:42,653
I told you my name is Darby, understand?

268
00:16:42,780 --> 00:16:44,740
Not Obi, not Barbie. Hmm?

269
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:46,990
Apologies.

270
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:52,377
He's screwing up his name on purpose to
get him riled up and throw off his game.

271
00:16:52,460 --> 00:16:54,097
I gotta hand it to the old man.

272
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:55,080
He's a natural.

273
00:16:55,780 --> 00:16:57,837
So what do you say we keep playing?

274
00:16:57,920 --> 00:17:01,200
I believe it's your turn
to drop a coin in, Darby!

275
00:17:11,060 --> 00:17:13,825
The shadow makes it
difficult to see from here.

276
00:17:14,340 --> 00:17:17,237
I'll lower the coin in from
the right side of the table.

277
00:17:17,320 --> 00:17:19,777
Drop it in from whatever angle you'd like.

278
00:17:19,860 --> 00:17:24,497
What he doesn't know is the glass is already
at its limit thanks to my little trick.

279
00:17:24,580 --> 00:17:27,497
There's no way the liquid
could take another coin.

280
00:17:27,580 --> 00:17:30,698
Even the slightest touch
will cause it to spill over.

281
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:41,557
You're probably thinking the
glass has reached its limit,

282
00:17:41,640 --> 00:17:44,581
that dropping in another
coin would be impossible.

283
00:17:45,980 --> 00:17:48,120
Well, you'd be wrong about that.

284
00:17:56,640 --> 00:17:57,920
There's no way!

285
00:17:58,140 --> 00:17:59,800
How the hell did he do that?

286
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:01,511
Why didn't it spill over?

287
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:03,289
Your question's confusing.

288
00:18:03,620 --> 00:18:05,037
What do you mean, why didn't it spill?

289
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:07,720
You saw the result with your own eyes.

290
00:18:08,840 --> 00:18:11,664
As far as I know, he
didn't do anything devious.

291
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:14,075
I was watching him with Star Platinum.

292
00:18:14,480 --> 00:18:17,717
It's hard to believe, but he
dropped it in fair and square.

293
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:18,800
There's no doubt.

294
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:21,500
But how did he do it?

295
00:18:21,880 --> 00:18:24,197
I'm positive I added enough liquid to the

296
00:18:24,280 --> 00:18:26,537
glass that one more coin
would make it spill.

297
00:18:26,620 --> 00:18:27,680
I don't get it.

298
00:18:27,840 --> 00:18:29,897
There's no way it shouldn't have spilled.

299
00:18:29,980 --> 00:18:31,180
What's going on?

300
00:18:31,560 --> 00:18:32,540
Make your move.

301
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:34,252
It's your turn, Joestar.

302
00:18:34,800 --> 00:18:38,780
Hurry it up already, or are you
trying to wait until it evaporates?

303
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:52,860
No, no, this can't be happening!

304
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:21,660
Oh, Mr. Jostar!

305
00:19:27,820 --> 00:19:29,377
Deep in his heart of hearts,

306
00:19:29,460 --> 00:19:33,377
Jostar had already come to the
realization that he'd lost this game.

307
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:36,000
That's why his soul emerged so easily.

308
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:39,464
I, Darby, have won this
bet like all the others.

309
00:19:41,900 --> 00:19:42,737
Polareff, I...

310
00:19:42,820 --> 00:19:43,820
I failed you.

311
00:19:44,280 --> 00:19:48,760
Ollie, I'm so sorry, my beautiful
girl, but Daddy's let you down.

312
00:19:51,740 --> 00:19:53,740
Mr. Joestar! Old man, no!

313
00:20:02,260 --> 00:20:03,140
Two down.

314
00:20:03,420 --> 00:20:06,620
Now let's continue where
we left off. That is,

315
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:09,057
unless you two have decided
to abandon your friends

316
00:20:09,140 --> 00:20:12,022
and slink away with your
tails between your legs.

317
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:13,860
You bastard!

318
00:20:16,380 --> 00:20:17,960
You don't get it, do you?

319
00:20:18,200 --> 00:20:22,937
I keep trying to tell you that if you take
my life, your friends will die with me.

320
00:20:23,020 --> 00:20:23,860
Damn you!

321
00:20:24,060 --> 00:20:25,520
Dantol, stand down! Hey,

322
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:26,917
if you're gonna cause trouble,

323
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:30,237
then I'm gonna have to ask you to leave
- Shut your mouth and stay out of this!

324
00:20:30,320 --> 00:20:31,150
Right!

325
00:20:47,360 --> 00:20:49,760
You've noticed it too late, Jotaro.

326
00:20:51,080 --> 00:20:51,910
What?

327
00:20:51,993 --> 00:20:52,857
Something's wrong with the glass?

328
00:20:52,940 --> 00:20:55,997
This is the reason the coin
didn't make the boost spill over.

329
00:20:56,080 --> 00:20:57,857
If you look at the bottom of the glass,

330
00:20:57,940 --> 00:21:00,877
you'll see that there's a
tiny bit of chocolate on it.

331
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:03,737
He must have found a way to stick
it on when he was inspecting

332
00:21:03,820 --> 00:21:06,996
the glass and coins at the
very beginning of the game.

333
00:21:07,540 --> 00:21:09,357
Surely you know the rules by now.

334
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:12,597
It doesn't count as cheating if
you never get caught in the act.

335
00:21:12,680 --> 00:21:13,510
What?

336
00:21:13,593 --> 00:21:14,423
I don't understand.

337
00:21:14,506 --> 00:21:18,117
How could a piece of chocolate
allow him to drop in an extra coin?

338
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:19,977
Well, at this point, it's melted.

339
00:21:20,060 --> 00:21:23,884
But it used to be a solid chunk
stuck to the bottom of the glass.

340
00:21:24,140 --> 00:21:26,337
Just enough to slightly tilt the glass,

341
00:21:26,420 --> 00:21:28,817
but not quite enough for
us to notice the change.

342
00:21:28,900 --> 00:21:33,457
Once the chocolate started to melt, the
glass came to be level with the table.

343
00:21:33,540 --> 00:21:36,157
With the glass leveled out,
the booze began to settle,

344
00:21:36,240 --> 00:21:38,593
which made enough room for another coin.

345
00:21:39,240 --> 00:21:40,560
What the hell?

346
00:21:41,180 --> 00:21:42,857
But that doesn't make any sense.

347
00:21:42,940 --> 00:21:46,697
How could he have known the chocolate
would melt right when he needed it to?

348
00:21:46,780 --> 00:21:49,015
He influenced things by using the sun.

349
00:21:49,200 --> 00:21:50,435
It slipped my notice.

350
00:21:51,140 --> 00:21:53,237
When he moved to the
right side of the table,

351
00:21:53,320 --> 00:21:55,857
he allowed the sun to shine
directly onto the chocolate,

352
00:21:55,940 --> 00:21:57,058
thereby melting it.

353
00:22:08,480 --> 00:22:09,310
Alright.

354
00:22:09,393 --> 00:22:12,120
Darby, get your cards,
cause we're playing my game.

355
00:22:12,380 --> 00:22:14,321
Hope you're ready for some poker.

356
00:22:14,680 --> 00:22:15,720
Say what?

357
00:22:16,320 --> 00:22:17,150
Jotaro!

358
00:22:18,740 --> 00:22:19,570
Interesting.

359
00:22:19,720 --> 00:22:23,957
You couldn't have possibly known this,
but poker is my absolute favorite game.

360
00:22:24,040 --> 00:22:25,511
Are you out of your mind?

361
00:22:25,600 --> 00:22:27,957
You're playing poker with
a man who outsmarted Mr.

362
00:22:28,040 --> 00:22:28,870
Joestar.

363
00:22:28,953 --> 00:22:29,783
It's too dangerous.

364
00:22:29,866 --> 00:22:30,700
Yeah, I know.

365
00:22:31,420 --> 00:22:33,917
Even though he doesn't
use physical strength,

366
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:37,059
he's the most dangerous
stand user we've ever faced.

367
00:22:37,860 --> 00:22:39,060
So now...

368
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:46,979
There's no turning back and
we're playing for keeps.
